16 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Diagram showing parts of a study on HIV-1 rebound in mice. Panel A outlines the experimental timeline involving HIV-1 infection, SECH cycles, and withdrawal. Panel B displays graphs of blood HIV-1 mRNA levels before and after SECH and ART withdrawal. Panel C presents UMAP plots of cell types across treatment conditions, with a color-coded legend for different T cell types. Panel D features a bar graph of pathway analysis for Gag positive cells in SECH-HIV positive mice, highlighting processes like transcription regulation and epigenetic modification.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (A composite scientific figure with four panels. Panel A shows a pair of scatter plots comparing gene expression between SECH-HIV positive and negative groups across various clusters, highlighting genes like RAB3A and ATG7. Panel B illustrates violin plots of expression levels for genes ATG7, ATG5, ATG10, ATG14, BNIP3L, and GABARAPL1 across different treatment groups, with significant differences indicated. Panel C presents fluorescent microscopy images of spleen cells, showing markers like CD4, p24, and LC3, with a graph quantifying LC3 puncta in p24 positive cells. Panel D displays similar data for liver cells with corresponding microscopy images and graph. Scale bars are included.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a ridge plot illustrating normalized enrichment scores \(NES\) for various metabolic processes with p-values indicating significance. Panel B presents a volcano plot comparing log2 fold changes and significance of gene expressions, highlighting specific genes. Panel C features violin plots displaying expression levels of metabolic genes like PKM and ALDOA under different conditions. Panel D depicts bar graphs showing percentage cell death across multiple treatments and HIV conditions, with significance indicated by asterisks.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (A: A circular diagram displays gene expression categories, each represented by different colors. Categories include histone methylation, acetylation, and demethylation activities, among others. B: Two scatter plots show gene expression analysis, comparing Gag-positive and Gag-negative samples. Specific genes like MECP2 and BRD4 are highlighted. C: Multiple violin plots depict expression levels of genes such as BRD4, BRDT, and MECP2 across different conditions, with significant differences marked by asterisks.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (A composite of scientific graphs and data visualizations showing the effects of various inhibitors on HIV-1 mRNA expression and cell death in CD4+ T cells. Panel A displays a bar graph comparing HIV-1 mRNA levels after treatment with different siRNAs, highlighting a significant increase with BRD4. Panel B shows percentage cell death under various conditions, noting statistical significance with HIV-1 infection and different treatments. Panels C, D, and E include ChIP assay results demonstrating BRD4 binding at the 5' LTR region under different conditions. Panel F presents a bar graph showing the effect of JQ1 and MS417 on HIV-1 mRNA levels. Panel G illustrates cell death percentages with various combinations of inhibitors and HIV-1. Statistical significance is indicated with asterisks.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a dot plot of gene expression for anti-apoptosis and pro-apoptosis markers across clusters. Panel B presents a heatmap illustrating expression levels in various clusters. Panel C displays violin plots showing expression levels of specific genes in anti-apoptosis and pro-apoptosis categories across different clusters. Panel D provides UMAP visualizations for each gene, highlighting expression patterns in low-dimensional space.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
